---
/**
 * Cyclist direction proposals: both riders, both kits, three views, at
 * display size and enlarged. The sheets come from `art/build.mjs`.
 */
import { withBase } from '../../i18n/routes.ts';

const CELL = { width: 76, height: 78 };
const views = ['Side', 'Front three-quarter', 'Rear three-quarter'];
const sheets = [
  { file: 'proposal-female-club.png', rider: 'Rider A', kit: 'Club kit' },
  { file: 'proposal-female-national.png', rider: 'Rider A', kit: 'Czech colours' },
  { file: 'proposal-male-club.png', rider: 'Rider B', kit: 'Club kit' },
  { file: 'proposal-male-national.png', rider: 'Rider B', kit: 'Czech colours' },
];
const frame = (file: string, index: number, zoom: number) =>
  `width:${CELL.width * zoom}px;height:${CELL.height * zoom}px;background:url(${withBase(`/art/${file}`)}) -${index * CELL.width * zoom}px 0 / ${CELL.width * 3 * zoom}px ${CELL.height * zoom}px no-repeat;image-rendering:pixelated`;
---

<div class="prose mb-10">
  <p>
    These are direction proposals, not finished sprites. I draw the riders from one posable model, so every view shares the same
    proportions, wheel centres and ground anchor. That is what will let the same rider turn through eight directions later
    without changing shape. Kits are palette swaps, so both riders wear both kits.
  </p>
  <p>What I need from you: are the proportions, the level of detail and the two kits the right direction?</p>
</div>

<h2>At display size</h2>
<p class="mb-4 text-ink-soft">Three screen pixels per art pixel, on the hero sky and grass colours.</p>
<div class="mb-12 overflow-x-auto border-2 border-ink">
  <div class="min-w-max bg-sky-2">
    {sheets.map((sheet) => (
      <div class="flex items-end gap-2 px-4 pt-2">
        {views.map((_, index) => <div role="img" aria-label={`${sheet.rider}, ${sheet.kit}, ${views[index]}`} style={frame(sheet.file, index, 3)} />)}
        <p class="mb-6 ml-4 max-w-none text-sm font-semibold">{sheet.rider} · {sheet.kit}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
    <div class="h-6 bg-grass-1"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Enlarged pixel detail</h2>
<p class="mb-4 text-ink-soft">Six screen pixels per art pixel.</p>
{sheets.filter((_, index) => index === 0 || index === 3).map((sheet) => (
  <figure class="mb-8">
    <figcaption class="mb-2 font-semibold">{sheet.rider} · {sheet.kit}</figcaption>
    <div class="border-2 border-ink bg-sky-2">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-around">
        {views.map((view, index) => (
          <div>
            <div role="img" aria-label={`${sheet.rider}, ${sheet.kit}, ${view}, enlarged`} style={frame(sheet.file, index, 6)} class="max-w-full" />
            <p class="max-w-none pb-2 text-center text-sm">{view}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>
))}

<h2>Kits</h2>
<ul class="prose mb-10">
  <li><strong>Club kit:</strong> an original design in the site colours, burnt orange and deep teal with a cream band.</li>
  <li><strong>Czech colours:</strong> an original white, red and blue design. It carries no federation or team marks.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Known gaps</h2>
<ul class="prose">
  <li>Faces, hands and the drivetrain are still schematic. They get hand-finished pixels once the direction is approved.</li>
  <li>Only the riding pose is shown. Carrying, running, remounting and the wave come with the motion work.</li>
  <li>The two riders differ in build and hair only. Tell me if you want them further apart.</li>
</ul>
